[06:19] I built and saved the phone agent, but it has not been tested on any calls. `public-test-set.json` is empty for this brief, so there were no practice customers to run. Its only tests are the workflow check (0 errors, 0 warnings, also on the copy the platform stored) and a local run of the date code.
[06:19] 
[06:19] **How I read the memos.** The brief says memos change the policy from their own date on, and anything dated before the policy is replaced by it.
[06:19] - **OM-3 (3 Feb 2026)** is older than the policy (2 Mar 2026), so I ignored it. That drops its 20:00 callback limit and its car-loan rule.
[06:19] - **OM-17 (9 Oct 2026)** applies from its date. Callbacks are booked 09:00–17:00, and the late band (8 to 45 days) gets the 6th business day as deadline. For a `now` before 9 Oct, the agent falls back to 10:00–19:00 and the 7th business day.
[06:19] - **`add_note`** is a Brief B tool and is not used.
[06:19] 
[06:19] **How the call is controlled.**
[06:19] - Code computes the dates from `now`: deadlines with bank holidays, callback slots, the date for persuasion attempt 1, and a calendar that resolves "this/next Friday". The agent gets a list of every date it may record.
[06:19] - Each way a call can end sends its own fixed `close_call` values and plays a fixed goodbye.
[06:19] - A recorded promise wins over any other ending except a later transfer. Three wrong identity answers always end as `not_verified` / `failed`.
[06:19] - Persuasion attempts are counted by the workflow itself, not by the prompt. A flat refusal moves to the next attempt, and when the attempts run out the call closes as `no_promise` / `refused`.
[06:19] - The workflow, not the model, decides when to leave a step after `verify_identity`, `create_promise`, `schedule_callback` and transfer results. A second failed `create_promise` closes as `no_promise` / `service_error` and says the promise was not recorded.
[06:19] 
[06:19] **Gaps you should know about:**
[06:19] - **Policy wording I filled in myself:**
[06:19]   - If `get_account` fails, the call closes as `no_promise` / `service_error`.
[06:19]   - If booking a callback fails, the agent tries once more.
[06:19] - **Only the model decides these, so they are untested:** classifying who answered, spotting a flat refusal, and choosing the paid, dispute, hardship or declined endings.
[06:19] - **Not handled:** a request for a human before the customer has confirmed who they are is not covered at the opening step.
[06:19] 
[06:19] The generator script is `gen/gen_body.py`. The files are in `out/`: `pl-g5-memo-raw.body.json`, `pl-g5-memo-raw.closing.json` and `pl-g5-memo-raw.workflow.json`.
